#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068559 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068705 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b04beff-987b-504f-9783-4465474e01ab" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Solutions"}] :question/id #uuid "d659780a-f726-5827-a13a-a64b21a0cf41" :question/math-academy-id "e-4027" :question/problem "What are the solutions to $x^2 + 16 = 0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\tx^2 + 16 &= 0 \\[3pt]\n\t\tx^2 &= -16\n}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = \\pm \\sqrt{-16}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $x$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pm \\sqrt{-16} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{16\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{16}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x = \\pm 4 \\textrm{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068560 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068706 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "386bce9a-0c89-545c-b9ed-b9f67fb836b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Solutions With Simplification"}] :question/id #uuid "8082e3bd-04dc-5598-93c5-dbc423cdba97" :question/math-academy-id "e-4028" :question/problem "If $p^2 + 27 = 0,$ then $p =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\np^2 + 27 & = 0\\[3pt]\n\np^2 & = -27 \n}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\np = \\pm \\sqrt{-27}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $p$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\\pm \\sqrt{-27} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{27\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{27}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{{3}^{2}\\cdot 3}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $p = \\pm 3\\sqrt{3} \\, \\textrm{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068561 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068707 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "701015d7-cc6a-52ff-b40d-627a640cd0fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Fractional Solutions"}] :question/id #uuid "99f522f8-39ff-5612-86d1-84e703bde35f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4029" :question/problem "If $16z^2 + 49 = 0,$ then $z =$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n16z^2 + 49 & = 0\\[5pt]\n\n16z^2 & = -49 \\[5pt]\n\nz^2 & = -\\dfrac{49}{16}\n}\n$$\n\nBy taking the square root, we obtain\n\n$$\nz = \\pm \\sqrt{-\\dfrac{49}{16}}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $z$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{49}{16}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{16}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{49}{16}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{49}}{\\sqrt{16}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{7}{4}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $z=\\pm \\dfrac{7}{4} \\textrm{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068562 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068708 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc45bf8f-2f0f-5ab9-b7d4-e9a3300b52a6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Fractional Roots With Solutions"}] :question/id #uuid "93aec687-49af-55ea-9212-b33dd29f4ce7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4030" :question/problem "What are the solutions of the equation $2y^2 + 9 = 0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t2y^2 + 9 &= 0 \\[5pt]\n\n\t\t2y^2 &= -9\\[5pt]\n\ny^2 & = -\\dfrac{9}{2}\n}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain\n\n$$\ny = \\pm \\sqrt{-\\dfrac{9}{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit $\\textrm{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\, \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{9}{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $y=\\pm \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\textrm{i}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068706 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "386bce9a-0c89-545c-b9ed-b9f67fb836b2" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Solutions With Simplification"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "082df12d-a520-52a4-a79f-c0349cc96c96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517505} {:answer/id #uuid "4ed1bc14-82fb-5586-8801-a9b3e6b4e62f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517642} {:answer/id #uuid "5cff7245-7201-59d9-87b6-8026bdec1e7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517658} {:answer/id #uuid "6d2fa09f-bb3c-500a-95e5-cd60c937e500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 2\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517697} {:answer/id #uuid "ef11576a-065b-5597-a05f-5c52d3c4c3c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d2fa09f-bb3c-500a-95e5-cd60c937e500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 2\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517697} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d2ce979-7e0d-5596-bf06-3e1a04e2c43e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "77b8b796-0079-55bf-a33c-a1e9a651dc45" :question/math-academy-id "q-112361" :question/problem "If $\\frac{{w}^{2}}{4}+22=0,$ then $w=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{w}^{2}}{4}+22 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{{w}^{2}}{4} & =-22 \\\\ {w}^{2} & =-88\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nw=\\pm \\sqrt{-88}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $w$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w & =\\pm \\sqrt{-88} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{88\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{88}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{22}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{22}\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518128 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068707 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "701015d7-cc6a-52ff-b40d-627a640cd0fb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Fractional Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "969f1e9e-4b76-5c2c-bf53-cb282cd406bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517773} {:answer/id #uuid "bcfad2dd-2a87-5e60-8f2d-670b7ad0671e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{8}{5}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517846} {:answer/id #uuid "cf368447-cb6f-5846-b336-75bdcf7ac676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{8}}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517878} {:answer/id #uuid "f0556a39-a30a-5103-8ac8-b9fd9c124181" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517947} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a37dfe-add9-5f03-af56-5005240e24ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "969f1e9e-4b76-5c2c-bf53-cb282cd406bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517773} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ba00ab0-0740-5e8c-a650-8814201a3289" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "400405cc-0be2-5aff-a15c-d39026e0c0e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-112392" :question/problem "Solve the equation $64{x}^{2}+25=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}64{x}^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ 64{x}^{2} & =-25 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-\\frac{25}{64}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nx=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{25}{64}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $x$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{25}{64}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{64}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{25}{64}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{\\sqrt{64}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{5}{8}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518133 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068708 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc45bf8f-2f0f-5ab9-b7d4-e9a3300b52a6" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Fractional Roots With Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c8d2c96-bf75-5f7c-985e-6f68a2e4ae27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{9}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517515} {:answer/id #uuid "93f2873d-9ebc-5f6a-8df6-69bfb7ebcbba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517767} {:answer/id #uuid "a4da0f14-5e09-529a-95ca-9379f4a7f02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{3}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517796} {:answer/id #uuid "b56fdb14-e345-575d-98f5-ff9d20c0bf6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{3}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517830} {:answer/id #uuid "e8c03e9a-9191-5060-bf9e-79f75effd569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{9}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b56fdb14-e345-575d-98f5-ff9d20c0bf6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{3}\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517830} :answer-field/id #uuid "e455b236-f5ba-5efb-9cf8-947f74de5bc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518082}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4f3f1aa3-5d05-5a94-a6c1-299187fd64c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-113227" :question/problem "What are the solutions of the equation $27{y}^{2}+63=0?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27{y}^{2}+63 & =0 \\\\ 27{y}^{2} & =-63 \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{63}{27} \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{7}{3}}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $y$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{7}{3}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{7}{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{3}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518139 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068705 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b04beff-987b-504f-9783-4465474e01ab" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "266bfaba-e0ad-54ed-a64f-4f4ffbfb8902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 5\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517559} {:answer/id #uuid "4b1ab51e-19e4-5940-bf86-98f1edbcd396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517634} {:answer/id #uuid "ac9eda6d-045e-5a51-b62d-88f1c1e340cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517808} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e8a1fd-a135-5c2b-9ac9-41a7a4d9916c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517900} {:answer/id #uuid "e1ec939f-0273-5f44-8255-e8b1ba57b46b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "266bfaba-e0ad-54ed-a64f-4f4ffbfb8902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 5\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517559} :answer-field/id #uuid "034b99ab-70ba-5ad6-bd7c-9dda87ca0e9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517970}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "54e8fcf4-d538-5483-805d-02e6f387fbe1" :question/math-academy-id "q-3798" :question/problem "Determine the solutions of the equation ${f}^{2}=-25.$" :question/worked-solution "By taking square root, we obtain:\n\n$$\nf=\\pm \\sqrt{-25}\n$$\n\nWe now rewrite $f$ using the imaginary unit $\\text{i}=\\sqrt{-1}\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f & =\\pm \\sqrt{-25} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{25\\cdot (-1)} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{25}\\cdot \\sqrt{-1} \\\\  & =\\pm 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518151 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068705 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b04beff-987b-504f-9783-4465474e01ab" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Quadratic Equation With Purely Imaginary Solutions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d188e9b-c8ce-5dcf-9c36-a3861cf5517e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517518} {:answer/id #uuid "42a6b18e-fce9-5676-9bb3-b8c41c919f98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517619} {:answer/id #uuid "6e10b4a5-c145-5f33-bc00-5b55f1b12b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pm 4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517700} {:answer/id #uuid "b3bbdea5-c901-5b65-a473-79724ef31de3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921860